/ActualText (Product Designer - Springworks\nDec 2020 - Aug 2026\nOwned end-to-end product design across B2B and enterprise products, from discovery and problem framing through user flows, prototyping, UI design, validation, and engineering handoff.\n Partnered with Product, Engineering, Operations, and client-facing teams to translate ambiguous requirements into scalable workflows and product experiences.\n Designed complex operational workflows across verification, vendor management, approvals, configuration, dashboards, and multi-step processes.\n Conducted user and stakeholder research to identify workflow gaps, validate assumptions, and inform product direction.\n Established reusable UI patterns and contributed to consistent design systems across multiple product experiences.\n Used AI-assisted workflows for research synthesis, exploration, prototyping, edge-case analysis, and faster iteration.\nSelected projects \(Springverify \(Enterprise Background Verification Platform\) \023 \nDesigned complex operational workflows across vendor management, verification, approvals, and escalation, simplifying fragmented processes for Operations and client-facing teams.\(Albus \(AI Workplace Assistant\) \023\(Designed conversational and action-based experiences inside Slack, enabling users to search information and execute workflows across connected tools such as Jira and CRM.\(EngageWith \(Employee Engagement Platform\) \023 \nDesigned recognition and rewards experiences, including Slack and Microsoft Teams integrations for real-time peer recognition.\nEZ Drafts \(Real Estate Contract Drafting Tool\) \023 \nDefined the product's visual language and designed workflows for creating, managing, and customizing complex real-estate agreements.)
/K [7]
/S /Span
/Type /StructElem
/P 860 0 R
/Pg 5 0 R
>>
